Reddit video improvement: Skua decodes the embed player's source objects by field
name rather than JSON member order. A 2026-10-23 live probe found that upstream's
order-dependent matcher missed Reddit's combined audio/video rendition and fell
back to a video-only CMAF rendition. The Go implementation recovers the combined
signed MP4 without copying upstream's parser or running a media transcoder.

upstreams.json records source revisions reviewed by a person. The maintenance
workflow reports later commits and open contributions but never executes them.

Kick clip support queries Kick's first-party public website API. URL shapes and
field names were cross-checked against yt-dlp's Kick extractor at the revision
in upstreams.json (Unlicense). No yt-dlp runtime or extractor code is copied.

HLS audio/video is repackaged by bluenviron/mediacommon v2.9.6 (MIT), using its
MPEG-TS reader and fragmented MP4 writer. Its original license is preserved in
LICENSE-mediacommon. Synthetic H.264 test parameters are from that project's
MIT-licensed test cases; source-authored clip content is not kept in fixtures.
The existing upstream watcher tracks both Kick extraction and media libraries.
